  "notes": "Cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; category kept 'provisional' though narrative describes clear human-performance causal factors (success bias, lack of understanding of drawer/relay interaction). CT-2 and standby buses/CT-5 remained powered throughout and are design-context/unaffected paths, not modeled as backups since MFB de-energization itself was resolved by breaker reclosure before KHU power reached the bus; KHS is modeled as backup since it actuated as designed per the automatic emergency function. C SFP and C LPSW pumps briefly lost power but were quickly restored; no separate consequence node created for these since narrative treats them as part of the same brief de-energization event."
